WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.791 --> 00:00:31.541
<b>In the previous verse,</b>

2
00:00:31.541 --> 00:00:40.875
<b>Lord Krishna explained how an enlightened </b>
<b>person responds internally to life's events.</b>

3
00:00:40.875 --> 00:00:42.000
<b>Now, He</b>

4
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.375
<b>describes such a person's external reactions.</b>

5
00:00:46.375 --> 00:00:49.791
<b>These are the answers to Arjuna's questions.</b>

6
00:00:49.791 --> 00:00:51.083
<b>Lord Krishna says that</b>

7
00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:52.833
<b>a person of steady wisdom:</b>

8
00:00:52.833 --> 00:00:57.875
<b>Remains detached in both </b>
<b>good and bad circumstances,</b>

9
00:00:57.875 --> 00:01:04.500
<b>Neither considers anything or </b>
<b>anyone as favorable or unfavorable,</b>

10
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.250
<b>nor harbors love or hatred towards them.</b>

11
00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:11.208
<b>Their intellect remains steady.</b>

12
00:01:16.041 --> 00:01:17.458
<b>Normally,</b>

13
00:01:17.458 --> 00:01:22.333
<b>when we experience something </b>
<b>pleasant or painful in life,</b>

14
00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:26.125
<b>various emotions arise within us,</b>

15
00:01:26.125 --> 00:01:30.916
<b>and we express these emotions through words.</b>

16
00:01:30.916 --> 00:01:33.625
<b>In this verse, Krishna explains</b>

17
00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:39.583
<b>that when something favorable or </b>
<b>auspicious happens to an enlightened person,</b>

18
00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:43.083
<b>they don't overly praise it,</b>

19
00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:44.041
<b>and</b>

20
00:01:44.041 --> 00:01:48.291
<b>when something unfavorable </b>
<b>or inauspicious occurs,</b>

21
00:01:48.291 --> 00:01:51.250
<b>they don't criticize it.</b>

22
00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:56.416
<b>If someone does them a favor, </b>
<b>they are certainly grateful,</b>

23
00:01:56.416 --> 00:02:00.958
<b>but they don't become </b>
<b>attached to the benefactor</b>

24
00:02:00.958 --> 00:02:05.166
<b>or expect anything more from them.</b>

25
00:02:05.166 --> 00:02:06.291
<b>Similarly,</b>

26
00:02:06.291 --> 00:02:08.250
<b>if someone insults them,</b>

27
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:15.500
<b>they neither accept the insult </b>
<b>nor speak ill of that person.</b>

28
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:21.125
<b>A person of steady wisdom</b>
<b>understands that good and bad,</b>

29
00:02:21.125 --> 00:02:25.875
<b>favorable and unfavorable </b>
<b>these are merely natural parts of life.</b>

30
00:02:25.875 --> 00:02:27.916
<b>These will come and go,</b>

31
00:02:27.916 --> 00:02:28.791
<b>but</b>

32
00:02:28.791 --> 00:02:32.250
<b>they themselves are an eternal soul.</b>

33
00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:37.333
<b>And what concern do eternal matters </b>
<b>have with these worldly circumstances?</b>

34
00:02:37.333 --> 00:02:40.750
<b>For them, this life is merely a </b>
<b>stopover on their spiritual journey</b>

35
00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.500
<b>a path to reach their spiritual goal,</b>

36
00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.583
<b>to unite with the Divine.</b>

37
00:02:45.583 --> 00:02:49.375
<b>And they remain focused on this purpose.</b>

38
00:02:49.375 --> 00:02:53.125
<b>Due to this singular focus on </b>
<b>their spiritual purpose, </b>

39
00:02:53.125 --> 00:02:59.458
<b>they remain unaffected by any good or bad </b>
<b>circumstances around them.</b>

40
00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:01.500
<b>They remain steady</b>

41
00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:06.041
<b>and continue performing their duties </b>
<b>while moving toward their spiritual goal.</b>

42
00:03:10.958 --> 00:03:13.458
<b>Typically,</b>

43
00:03:13.458 --> 00:03:17.250
<b>when something unpleasant happens in life,</b>

44
00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:21.125
<b>people instinctively cry out</b>

45
00:03:21.125 --> 00:03:24.541
<b>"Why does this always happen to me?"</b>

46
00:03:24.541 --> 00:03:27.708
<b>They start placing blame</b>

47
00:03:27.708 --> 00:03:30.375
<b>sometimes on circumstances, </b>

48
00:03:30.375 --> 00:03:33.750
<b>sometimes on others,</b>

49
00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:41.125
<b>and often even hold God responsible.</b>

50
00:03:41.125 --> 00:03:46.166
<b>While these reactions yield nothing positive,</b>

51
00:03:46.166 --> 00:03:54.291
<b>they gradually make a person</b>
<b>bitter and discouraged.</b>

52
00:03:54.291 --> 00:03:58.125
<b>And once they've blamed others,</b>

53
00:03:58.125 --> 00:04:06.791
<b>it implies they've accepted they have no control.</b>

54
00:04:06.791 --> 00:04:13.541
<b>Consequently, they take no </b>
<b>concrete steps toward improvement.</b>

55
00:04:13.541 --> 00:04:20.541
<b>As a result, what follows is also unpleasant.</b>

56
00:04:20.541 --> 00:04:23.125
<b>The cycle begins again</b>

57
00:04:23.125 --> 00:04:24.458
<b>of despair,</b>

58
00:04:24.458 --> 00:04:25.833
<b>blame,</b>

59
00:04:25.833 --> 00:04:27.416
<b>and bitterness.</b>

60
00:04:27.416 --> 00:04:32.916
<b>Here, it's essential to repeat these</b>
<b>three statements to yourself:</b>

61
00:04:32.916 --> 00:04:34.583
<b>First</b>

62
00:04:34.583 --> 00:04:38.750
<b>No one else is responsible for my situation.</b>

63
00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.166
<b>Second</b>

64
00:04:40.166 --> 00:04:44.500
<b>Pleasant and unpleasant circumstances </b>
<b>don't happen to me alone;</b>

65
00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:47.958
<b>they happen to everyone.</b>

66
00:04:47.958 --> 00:04:49.625
<b>And third</b>

67
00:04:49.625 --> 00:04:54.458
<b>My actions are within my control.</b>

68
00:04:54.458 --> 00:05:03.666
<b>I should focus on what I can do to</b>
<b>improve the situation.</b>

69
00:05:03.666 --> 00:05:08.625
<b>This too is spiritual thinking, </b>
<b>where there's no bitterness,</b>

70
00:05:08.625 --> 00:05:10.250
<b>no blame-shifting,</b>

71
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:14.333
<b>only dedication to right action.</b>

72
00:05:19.083 --> 00:05:23.083
<b>When something good happens in life,</b>

73
00:05:23.083 --> 00:05:27.208
<b>people praise that time</b>

74
00:05:27.208 --> 00:05:31.083
<b>"Those days were so wonderful"</b>

75
00:05:31.083 --> 00:05:36.166
<b>you must have said or heard this too.</b>

76
00:05:36.166 --> 00:05:37.458
<b>Not just that,</b>

77
00:05:37.458 --> 00:05:44.291
<b>they praise those who supported them.</b>

78
00:05:44.291 --> 00:05:48.541
<b>Conversely, when something bad happens,</b>

79
00:05:48.541 --> 00:05:51.541
<b>they blame time</b>

80
00:05:51.541 --> 00:05:54.458
<b>"Those were bad days."</b>

81
00:05:54.458 --> 00:06:02.333
<b>And people don't escape blame either. </b>
<b>They too are held responsible.</b>

82
00:06:02.333 --> 00:06:03.750
<b>Let's</b>

83
00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.375
<b>first address time</b>

84
00:06:06.375 --> 00:06:07.708
<b>neither good</b>

85
00:06:07.708 --> 00:06:09.041
<b>nor bad,</b>

86
00:06:09.041 --> 00:06:11.250
<b>time is neutral.</b>

87
00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.500
<b>Just like</b>

88
00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:15.458
<b>rain is neutral.</b>

89
00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:19.416
<b>Rain pours the same water everywhere,</b>

90
00:06:19.416 --> 00:06:20.875
<b>but</b>

91
00:06:20.875 --> 00:06:24.708
<b>somewhere a mango plant sprouts,</b>

92
00:06:24.708 --> 00:06:29.083
<b>elsewhere a poisonous vine.</b>

93
00:06:29.083 --> 00:06:41.291
<b>What grows doesn't depend on the rain, </b>
<b>but on what seed you planted.</b>

94
00:06:41.291 --> 00:06:43.250
<b>Similarly,</b>

95
00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:48.041
<b>whether you sow seeds of good actions or bad,</b>

96
00:06:48.041 --> 00:06:53.000
<b>the resulting plant will grow accordingly.</b>

97
00:06:53.000 --> 00:07:01.416
<b>Time simply brings these </b>
<b>results before you impartially.</b>

98
00:07:01.416 --> 00:07:04.291
<b>Time isn't good or bad</b>

99
00:07:04.291 --> 00:07:09.250
<b>everything is just the result of your actions.</b>

100
00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:16.791
<b>When you understand this,</b>
<b>no situation will destabilize you.</b>

101
00:07:16.791 --> 00:07:17.791
<b>Because</b>

102
00:07:17.791 --> 00:07:23.958
<b>your actions are within your control.</b>

103
00:07:23.958 --> 00:07:31.583
<b>Change them completely, </b>
<b>and future results will change too.</b>

104
00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:34.625
<b>Regarding people</b>

105
00:07:34.625 --> 00:07:45.916
<b>haven't you seen how someone</b>
<b>praised yesterday becomes disliked today?</b>

106
00:07:45.916 --> 00:07:47.458
<b>And someone</b>

107
00:07:47.458 --> 00:07:52.500
<b>who seemed bad now appears good?</b>

108
00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:53.791
<b>And yes,</b>

109
00:07:53.791 --> 00:07:58.875
<b>if someone you dislike were truly bad,</b>

110
00:07:58.875 --> 00:08:02.250
<b>they wouldn't have any friends.</b>

111
00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.041
<b>But</b>

112
00:08:03.041 --> 00:08:08.125
<b>that's not the case.</b>

113
00:08:08.125 --> 00:08:15.500
<b>When you realize it's pointless to </b>
<b>discuss others' goodness or badness,</b>

114
00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:22.333
<b>when you stop unnecessarily</b>
<b>blaming others for your situation</b>

115
00:08:22.333 --> 00:08:27.583
<b>there will be no bitterness </b>
<b>in your heart for anyone.</b>

116
00:08:27.583 --> 00:08:32.666
<b>This too will help you in social settings.</b>

117
00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:43.708
<b>Ups and downs are an integral </b>
<b>part of any professional journey.</b>

118
00:08:43.708 --> 00:08:45.666
<b>This is natural,</b>

119
00:08:45.666 --> 00:08:52.000
<b>especially because every </b>
<b>business depends on many factors...</b>

120
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.916
<b>first</b>

121
00:08:53.916 --> 00:08:55.208
<b>you,</b>

122
00:08:55.208 --> 00:08:56.291
<b>but</b>

123
00:08:56.291 --> 00:09:00.916
<b>along with you, your customers, colleagues,</b>

124
00:09:00.916 --> 00:09:05.333
<b>rules and regulations, </b>
<b>and many other circumstances.</b>

125
00:09:05.333 --> 00:09:10.916
<b>The business outcome emerges</b>
<b>from the interaction of all these.</b>

126
00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:17.916
<b>Can you control such an outcome completely?</b>

127
00:09:17.916 --> 00:09:20.041
<b>No, right?</b>

128
00:09:20.041 --> 00:09:24.125
<b>Can you influence the outcome?</b>

129
00:09:24.125 --> 00:09:26.250
<b>Certainly you can.</b>

130
00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:30.541
<b>Through proper understanding, </b>
<b>knowing your customers' minds,</b>

131
00:09:30.541 --> 00:09:33.416
<b>keeping colleagues motivated,</b>

132
00:09:33.416 --> 00:09:37.125
<b>understanding rules and regulations well.</b>

133
00:09:37.125 --> 00:09:40.625
<b>You can do all these things, </b>

134
00:09:40.625 --> 00:09:46.708
<b>and they will definitely influence the results.</b>

135
00:09:46.708 --> 00:09:48.416
<b>However,</b>

136
00:09:48.416 --> 00:09:52.541
<b>if you try to maintain complete control,</b>

137
00:09:52.541 --> 00:09:54.958
<b>then during bad results,</b>

138
00:09:54.958 --> 00:10:01.625
<b>you'll either become discouraged</b>
<b>or blame others.</b>

139
00:10:01.625 --> 00:10:07.708
<b>Both reactions will negatively impact your work.</b>

140
00:10:07.708 --> 00:10:14.625
<b>Which will, in turn, negatively impact</b>
<b>your future results.</b>

141
00:10:14.625 --> 00:10:18.375
<b>Don't try to maintain complete control...</b>

142
00:10:18.375 --> 00:10:20.083
<b>neither in business</b>

143
00:10:20.083 --> 00:10:22.416
<b>nor in life.</b>

144
00:10:22.416 --> 00:10:25.666
<b>Be grateful in good results.</b>

145
00:10:25.666 --> 00:10:29.166
<b>Be patient in bad results,</b>

146
00:10:29.166 --> 00:10:30.833
<b>understand the situation,</b>

147
00:10:30.833 --> 00:10:35.083
<b>and do what's in your control</b>

148
00:10:35.083 --> 00:10:38.333
<b>and what is in your control?</b>

149
00:10:38.333 --> 00:10:40.083
<b>Your work,</b>

150
00:10:40.083 --> 00:10:42.333
<b>your actions.</b>

151
00:10:42.333 --> 00:10:44.708
<b>No success is final,</b>

152
00:10:44.708 --> 00:10:47.125
<b>no failure is fatal.</b>

153
00:10:47.125 --> 00:10:54.333
<b>Just keep moving forward with </b>
<b>the right values and perspective.</b>

